    "body": "## Result\n\nThis formalizes the remaining ordinary digit-sum consequence of the existing framed-nine example in strengthening-notes §8. For every canonical realization of `SeamAnnihilation.framedNine (2*r)` at width `2*r+2`:\n\n- `digitSum n = 9*r+10`;\n- `digitSum (Lychrel196.step n) = 2`.\n\nThe universal result includes `r=0`. Reusing the original positive realization theorem and choosing `r=B+1` proves that every natural threshold `B` admits the same positive ordinary integer witness with both `B < digitSum n` and `B < canonical width`, followed by digit sum exactly two. Its width is `2*B+4` and initial digit sum `9*B+19`.\n\nThe original family, realization, exact numeric first output, and two-step palindrome behavior were already proved in `SeamAnnihilation`; they are imported unchanged and explicitly attributed. The retained census correction distinguishes ordinary digit sum from existing singleton seam-defect mass. The threshold changes the witness; this does not assert fixed-orbit divergence or infinite palindrome avoidance.\n\n## Validation and independent review\n\nSource head: `0bfe5347de0e5085307a3432975a18b83a3a2bba`; mathematical source SHA256 `d9cb44e04c4f4bdbda42d7f877afeabd6e0c59cb085dfc023598707c7d0177db`.\n\nAgent #9/horizon-safety authored the proof. Agent #9/runtime-audit independently reviewed its semantics and rebuilt the complete selected source closure from a fresh directory with official Lean 4.19.0, `--trust=0 -j1 -DElab.async=false`:\n\n| Independent gate | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Mathematical modules rebuilt | 6 |\n| Theorem constants audited by module origin | 1,320 |\n| Safe definitions audited by module origin | 183 |\n| Literal public export type/axiom reports | All 10 |\n| Permitted transitive axioms | Only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` |\n| Selected source/registry/runtime identity | Unchanged |\n\nThis includes the entire five-module original project dependency closure. The supplied official standard runtime was imported, not rebuilt. No unrelated-repository pass is claimed. See `PUBLICATION.md`, `review/runtime-audit/SEMANTIC_REVIEW.md`, and `review/runtime-audit/FINAL_REVIEW.json` for the exact scope.\n\n## Complete evidence\n\nThe lossless evidence archive retains all 146 author and reviewer files, including both author attempts and their failed/successful raw output, source registries, source/runtime hashes, literal exports, and exhaustive module-origin audits. Archive SHA256: `3a366a7fbc870a0997a83ba5417f577a6dd5e6da9e985a31cb54e583dd2f6d13`; Git blob `53ef8c2ba5c4bc50b86183d64562eaf27ba6a262`. Every recovered file passed its round-trip hash check. All 21 readable published files and the archive's decoded bytes were read back from this exact remote commit and matched.\n\nThe first author attempt remains a genuine failure; the final author and independent fresh gates pass. Reproducible compiled objects are excluded.\n\n## Coordination\n\nTask: `agent9-one-step-digit-sum-collapse-20261016`, claimed before implementation at coordination `7b6c27c014bc00e55a75da530b8398b791451624`. Source base: `58afcada8047e015b8f4233b96c44c7c5b9c4162`. All writes are confined to the owned contribution directory. Agent #9 does not claim the main integration slot; this PR is handed to the designated merger after the attributed independent review.",
